{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-11767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-4,-6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,-6),$ we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-6)^{2} & =4p(-4) \\\\ 36 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{9}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-9x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25fc2a63ccb547609ccd88b96d2ba4646ed4dc26e2936e05de4d1f171bdd7563"} {"question" "q-11767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-3x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-6x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-9x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=6x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=9x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-9x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-7,-7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-7,-7),$ we can substitute $x=-7$ and $y=-7$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-7)^{2} & =4p(-7) \\\\ 49 & =-28p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{7}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25fc2a63ccb547609ccd88b96d2ba4646ed4dc26e2936e05de4d1f171bdd7563"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-3x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-5x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-7x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=5x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=7x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-7x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/assets/e4b681e9bdf5fa8021ca359e0bf93c27b53a18f0d5e906765a911a72ecfc0159.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(4,2)$ and passes through the point $(-8,10).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(4,2),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,10),$ so we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=10$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (10-2)^{2} & =4p(-8-4) \\\\ 64 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{4}{3})(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{4}{3}$ is negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25fc2a63ccb547609ccd88b96d2ba4646ed4dc26e2936e05de4d1f171bdd7563"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x-4)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)"] ["math" "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x-4)"] ["math" "(y-4)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11807" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/assets/ecf128d341a8a568ade4abaa2a59e1083d2c436fdb3d2a0b4b642fb7e85cee63.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(6,4)$ and passes through the point $(1,9).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(6,4),$ we substitute $h=6$ and $k=4$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(1,9),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=9$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6) \\\\ (9-4)^{2} & =4p(1-6) \\\\ 25 & =-20p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{5}{4})(x-6) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =-5(x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{5}{4}$ is negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25fc2a63ccb547609ccd88b96d2ba4646ed4dc26e2936e05de4d1f171bdd7563"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y-4)^{2}=-3(x-6)"] ["math" "(y-4)^{2}=-5(x-6)"] ["math" "(y-4)^{2}=3(x-6)"] ["math" "(y-4)^{2}=5(x-6)"] ["math" "(y-6)^{2}=-5(x-4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-11811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y-4)^{2}=-5(x-6)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-115648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,2)$ and passes through the point $(5,5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-115648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,2),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,5),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (5-2)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 9 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{20})x \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7af8b8942f4efddabc45c2f53eea749d3ae53fb0325359c565aba967bcf5738"} {"question" "q-115648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25fc2a63ccb547609ccd88b96d2ba4646ed4dc26e2936e05de4d1f171bdd7563"} {"question" "q-115648" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "ca